<title>PORTUGAL: Bank/Portugal sets repo, leaves rates steady.</title>
<headline>Bank/Portugal sets repo, leaves rates steady.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Portugal said it offered to inject 300 billion escudos into the money market in a variable rate repurchase pact effective tomorrow, and said that it had left the absorption and emergency lending rates steady.</p>
<p>Bids for the repo funds must be submitted by 1415 GMT. The central bank previously injected repo funds at an average weighted interest rate of 6.0070 percent.</p>
<p>The draining rate remains at 5.70 percent and the emergency lending rate at 7.70 percent.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
